E°_cell = E°_cathode - E°_anode = 0.34 V - 0.0 V = 0.34 V

The reaction quotient (Q) can be calculated using the concentrations and pressures of the species involved in the reaction:

Q = [Cu²⁺]/[H⁺]² * P(H₂)

Since the hydrogen electrode is under standard conditions, the concentration of H⁺ ions is 1 M and the pressure of H₂ gas is 1 bar:

