$$y = \frac{1}{4} \cdot 4^0 - 1$$
Since $4^0 = 1$, we have:
$$y = \frac{1}{4} \cdot 1 - 1$$
$$y = \frac{1}{4} - 1$$
$$y = 0.25 - 1$$
$$y = -0.75$$
The y-intercept is the point where the line or graph intersects the y-axis, which is when $x = 0$. In this case, the y-intercept is $y = -0.75$.

