What is the maximum percentage change in the wavelength of a 2.00 Å photon scattered by an electron?
</USER_REQUEST>

<GROUND_TRUTH>
The maximum percentage change in wavelength occurs when the photon is backscattered (θ = 180°). The Compton wavelength shift is given by:
\[
\Delta \lambda = \frac{2h}{m_e c} = 0.0486 \, \text{Å}
\]
The percentage change is:
\[
\frac{\Delta \lambda}{\lambda} \times 100 = \frac{0.0486}{2.00} \times 100 = 2.43\%
