(b) To find the time taken to reach \(35,000 \, \text{m/s}\):  
1. Using the kinematic equation \(v = u + at\), where \(u = 0\) (starts from rest), \(v = 35,000 \, \text{m/s}\), and \(a = 4.79 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2\):  
   \[
   t = \frac{v}{a} = \frac{35,000 \, \text{m/s}}{4.79 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2} = 7.31 \times 10^{-7} \, \text{s}
   \]  
   The time taken is \(\boxed{7.31 \times 10^{-7} \, \text{s}}\).  

